{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Collection Item","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404024","type":"Type"}],"id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/library/7286","identified_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"repository number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404621"}],"content":"7286","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"call number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300311706"}],"content":"PG3385 .G62 1920b","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"preferred term","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670"}],"content":"Reminiscences of Leo Nikolaevich Tolstoy  ","type":"Name"}],"produced_by":{"carried_out_by":[{"_label":"Gorky, Maksim,","id":"actor/gorky-maksim","type":"Actor"},{"_label":"B.W. Huebsch","id":"actor/b-w-huebsch","type":"Actor"}],"timespan":{"_label":"1920","begin_of_the_begin":"1920-01-01T00:00:00Z","end_of_the_end":"1920-01-01T00:00:00Z","type":"TimeSpan"},"type":"Production"},"referred_to_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"description statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"}],"content":"From Georgia O'Keeffe's Ghost Ranch library.","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"inscription statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435414"}],"content":"Bookseller sticker inside back cover : Brentano's / Booksellers \u0026 Stationers / New York.|grl copy : good condition ; dust jacket : good condition.|Inscription on front loose endpaper from Edward Dahlberg to Alfred Stieglitz, April 26, 1944 : For Alfred Stieglitz in his / 80th year - / Of all those who labored for / visionary bethlehems in / America - the Rappites, the Brook / Farmers, the Oneidans, the [Fruitlorlens], / the New Hammonites - \u0026 no matter how socialism, communism, utopianism / may appear, it has always been \u0026 / will always be caeserism / and Mammon - Stieglitz alone / toiled for the real communal spirit, / the Arts.  When the dust, the chaff / and the barley of the soul are / weighed in Job's Balance, Alfred / Stieglitz will be remembered / along with Sherwood Anderson, / Randolph Bourne, Marsden Hartley. / Long life my friend, / Edward Dahlberg, / N.Y.C. / Apr. 26 '44.","type":"LinguisticObject"}],"representation":[],"type":"HumanMadeObject"}